From cb425f3ca1a4f53fd840ab7807c33fd3424ade02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pdurlej <1210027+pdurlej@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:26:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(mcp,events): poll the event log by cursor over JSON and
 MCP

An MCP client, or anything that can't hold an SSE stream, can read the daemon's event log a page at a time from a
cursor: `GET /api/events/replay` and the `rig_events_replay` MCP tool. It is the log the SSE stream replays, read with
the stream's `replayPage`, not a second one.

- `GET /api/events/replay?since=&rigId=&limit=` returns up to `limit` events (default 200, at most 1000) after `since`,
  oldest first, with the `nextCursor` to pass as the next `since` and whether the page reached the newest event.
- A cursor whose next event is no longer stored answers 410 `cursor_expired` with the `resyncCursor` to continue from,
  on the JSON page and on the SSE stream (`Last-Event-ID`, or `?since=` for a client that can't set the header),
  instead of resuming across a silent gap. The log is never pruned today, so no client meets it yet.
- `rig_events_replay` takes a rig name or id, as the other rig tools do.
- The openrig-user skill and the as-built stack list the tool (24 MCP tools).
